IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa-interests`

-- Companies Act 1967, section 7 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.
-- The sixteen-field fixtures below are generated from a table of which flags are set,
-- so that a typing slip cannot make a case say something other than its name.

§ `Fixtures -- a person's own interest`

`authority only` MEANS PersonsInterest WITH
    `has authority, formal or informal, express or implied, to dispose of the shares or to control their disposal` IS TRUE
    `knows or has reasonable grounds for believing it has an interest under a trust whose property includes the shares` IS FALSE
    `has contracted to purchase a share` IS FALSE
    `has a right, other than as a trust beneficiary, to have a share transferred to it or its order` IS FALSE
    `has a right to acquire a share or an interest in a share under an option` IS FALSE
    `is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share it is not the registered holder of, other than as proxy or representative` IS FALSE
    `holds a book-entry security` IS FALSE
    `the interest is a unit in a collective investment scheme within section 7(3)` IS FALSE
    `holds the share as bare trustee` IS FALSE
    `lends money in the ordinary course of business and holds the interest only as security for such a transaction` IS FALSE
    `holds the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office` IS FALSE
    `is a company's interest in its own shares bought or acquired under sections 76B to 76G` IS FALSE
    `is a prescribed interest to be disregarded` IS FALSE
    `holds jointly with another person` IS FALSE
    `the interest cannot be related to any particular share` IS FALSE
    `the interest is remote, or arose in an unusual way, or is subject to restraint` IS FALSE

